---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import TermStage from "../../components/TermStage.astro";
import { getGuide } from "../../data/guides";

const guide = getGuide("cli");
---

<DocsLayout guide={guide}>
<section class="docs-hero docs-searchable" id="overview" data-search="cli command line reference scan report rules intelligence flags">
          <h1>CLI reference</h1>
          <p>Scan repositories, review findings, and export reports. Run <code>repyy help</code> for the commands and flags in your installed version.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="shape" data-search="command shape syntax subcommands targets path git url">
          <h2>Command shape</h2>
          <pre class="docs-example" aria-label="repyy command shape">
repyy
repyy scan [options] &lt;path-or-git-url&gt;...
repyy report [options] &lt;report.json|-&gt;
repyy report --format tui
repyy guard [scan options] [--format text|json] [--command CMD | -- CMD...]
repyy mcp [scan options]
repyy rules validate &lt;rules.yaml&gt;
repyy rules check
repyy rules list [--format terminal|json]
repyy rules catalog [--format terminal|json]
repyy rules explain &lt;rule-id&gt; [--format terminal|json]
repyy intel status [--format terminal|json]
repyy intel update
repyy intel rollback
repyy version</pre
          >
          <p>
            Flags can appear before or after targets. A value flag accepts either a space or an equals sign, for example <code>--format html</code> and
            <code>--format=html</code>. Boolean flags such as <code>--include-dependencies</code> do not take a value.
          </p>
          <p>
            <code>guard</code> and <code>mcp</code> connect Repyy to coding agents. Setup for each harness is in the
            <a href="/agent-skill/#mcp">agent integration guide</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="first-scan" data-search="install first local scan folder path example">
          <h2>Run a first scan</h2>
          <p>
            Run this from the directory that contains your checkout. Replace <code>./project</code> with its path.
          </p>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Local folder</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan ./project">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy scan ./project</code>
          </div>
          <p>
            A scan in an interactive terminal opens the <a href="#interactive-review">interactive review</a>. Use an absolute path when the target is elsewhere
            and quote paths containing spaces.
          </p>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Path with spaces</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan '/Users/me/Code/Take home assignment'">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy scan '/Users/me/Code/Take home assignment'</code>
          </div>
          <p>
            Remote targets are Git URLs. Host mode needs Git; HTTPS private remotes use the matching provider token in the process environment. Keep credentials
            out of URLs.
          </p>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Remote repository</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan https://github.com/org/repo">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy scan https://github.com/org/repo</code>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="interactive-review" data-search="tui interactive terminal review keyboard shortcuts findings coverage">
          <h2>Interactive review</h2>
          <p>
            Run <code>repyy</code> in a terminal to open Home, <code>repyy scan</code> to choose a target, or <code>repyy report</code> to pick a saved report.
            Interactive review is available in{" "}
            <a href="https://github.com/Kevin-Umali/repyy/releases/tag/v0.7.3">Repyy v0.7.3</a> and later.
          </p>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Scan and review</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan ./checkout --format tui">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy scan ./checkout --format tui</code>
          </div>
          <TermStage
            flow="inspect"
            caption="A replay of interactive review: open a finding with Enter, step to the next one with ], open the handoff brief with h, go back with Esc, and open the coverage tab with 3."
          />
          <p>
            Press <kbd>1</kbd>, <kbd>2</kbd>, or <kbd>3</kbd> to switch between findings, repositories, and coverage. Press <kbd>Enter</kbd> to open a finding,
            then <kbd>[</kbd> and <kbd>]</kbd> to step through the others without going back. Press <kbd>/</kbd> to search, <kbd>f</kbd> to filter by severity,
            <kbd>e</kbd> to export, or <kbd>?</kbd> for every key. You can also click tabs and rows and scroll with the mouse wheel.
          </p>
          <p>
            Press <kbd>y</kbd> to copy the selected finding's <code>file:line</code>, and <kbd>h</kbd> for a Markdown handoff brief you can paste into an issue
            or give to a coding agent; <kbd>y</kbd> copies the brief. The brief lists every finding, including those hidden by display options. Press
            <kbd>l</kbd> from a finding for evidence locations, <kbd>n</kbd> for session notes, and <kbd>t</kbd> for a five-minute reminder. <kbd>r</kbd> and
            <kbd>c</kbd> also open repositories and coverage. Press <kbd>Esc</kbd> to go back or <kbd>q</kbd> to exit.
          </p>
          <p>
            On Home, press <kbd>1</kbd> for the User workspace, <kbd>2</kbd> for Developer, or <kbd>3</kbd> for Agent, or choose a card with the arrow keys. These
            workspaces export to HTML, SARIF, and JSON by default. You can select a different format. If the destination exists, Repyy asks for another path.
          </p>
          <div class="terminal-review-examples">
            <figure>
              <figcaption>Choose a workspace in Home</figcaption>
              <a href="/images/terminal-home.png">
                <img
                  class="terminal-review-screenshot"
                  src="/images/terminal-home.png"
                  alt="Repyy Home: the repyy wordmark above three workspace cards, User, Developer and Agent. User is selected."
                  width="1000"
                  height="520"
                  loading="lazy"
                />
              </a>
            </figure>
            <figure>
              <figcaption>Open a finding with Enter</figcaption>
              <a href="/images/terminal-finding.png">
                <img
                  class="terminal-review-screenshot"
                  src="/images/terminal-finding.png"
                  alt="Finding 1 of 2: a critical finding for a remote download piped into a command interpreter, with its location, recommended action, evidence and rule."
                  width="1000"
                  height="600"
                  loading="lazy"
                />
              </a>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Open a saved scan</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy report scan.json --format tui">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy report scan.json --format tui</code>
          </div>
          <p>
            Interactive review requires terminal stdin and stdout. With those terminals, <code>scan</code> defaults to TUI when you omit <code>--format</code>
            and <code>--output</code> and <code>CI</code> is empty, <code>false</code>, or <code>0</code>. To request TUI explicitly in CI, pass
            <code>--format tui</code>. For redirected input or output, use a text or file format.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section
          class="docs-section docs-searchable"
          id="targets"
          data-search="targets multiple path url file target file comments blank lines jobs order history shallow clone"
        >
          <h2>Targets and target files</h2>
          <p>
            Pass one or more local directories and Git URLs. Command-line targets are processed first. Add <code>--file</code> to append a UTF-8 text list, one
            path or URL per line; blank lines and lines whose first non-whitespace character is <code>#</code> are ignored.
          </p>
          <pre class="docs-example" aria-label="Example targets.txt">
# Review queue
./assignment-a
https://github.com/org/assignment-b</pre
          >
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Several targets</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan ./repo-a ./repo-b --file targets.txt --jobs 4">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy scan ./repo-a ./repo-b --file targets.txt --jobs 4</code>
          </div>
          <p>
            <code>--jobs</code> controls concurrent repositories, from 1 through 128, with a default of 4. Docker uses no more than four effective workers.
            Remote history is shallow by default: use <code>--history 20</code> or <code>--history all</code> when earlier commits matter.
          </p>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Inspect history</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan https://github.com/org/repo --history 20">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy scan https://github.com/org/repo --history 20</code>
          </div>
          <p>
            Host-mode remote checkouts are temporary and removed after the scan. Add
            <code>--keep-workdir</code> to retain one for follow-up review. This option is rejected with Docker.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section
          class="docs-section docs-searchable"
          id="scan-flags"
          data-search="scan flags options defaults file format output jobs config dependencies history keep workdir sandbox fail timeout max files bytes detail progress color severity confidence group"
        >
          <h2>All <code>scan</code> flags</h2>
          <div class="flag-grid">
            <code>--file PATH</code><span>Append targets from a text file. One path or URL per line; blank and <code>#</code> comment lines are skipped.</span>
            <code>--format FORMAT</code><span>
              <code>tui</code>, <code>terminal</code>, <code>json</code>, <code>sarif</code>, or <code>html</code>. The default is <code>tui</code> during
              interactive use without <code>--output</code>, and <code>terminal</code> otherwise.
            </span>
            <code>--output PATH</code><span>Write a text or file format to a path such as <code>review.html</code>.</span>
            <code>--jobs N</code><span>Concurrent repositories, 1–128; default <code>4</code>. Docker caps effective concurrency at 4.</span>
            <code>--config PATH</code
            ><span>Load a reviewed version-1 YAML file with custom rules and suppressions. See <a href="../configuration/">configuration</a>.</span>
            <code>--include-dependencies</code
            ><span
              >Include dependency and cache trees such as <code>node_modules</code>, <code>.venv</code>, <code>vendor</code>, <code>target</code>, and
              <code>Pods</code>, which are skipped by default.</span
            >
            <code>--registry-check</code
            ><span
              >Look up declared npm and PyPI packages on their public registries and report new, rarely used, or missing packages (<code>PKG-010</code>,
              <code>PKG-011</code>). Off by default; sends package names to the registries. Unsupported with <code>--sandbox docker</code>.</span
            >
            <code>--history N|all</code><span>Remote Git history depth; default <code>1</code>. <code>all</code> requests full history.</span>
            <code>--keep-workdir</code><span>Keep a host-mode remote checkout. Unsupported with <code>--sandbox docker</code>.</span>
            <code>--sandbox host|docker</code
            ><span
              ><code>host</code> is default. Docker requires a running daemon and the verified release-matched image. <code>vm</code> and <code>auto</code> are
              unavailable.</span
            >
            <code>--fail-on LEVEL</code
            ><span>Exit 1 at or above <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code>, <code>high</code>, or <code>critical</code>; default <code>high</code>.</span>
            <code>--timeout DURATION</code
            ><span>Per-repository limit; default <code>10m</code>. Use positive durations such as <code>30s</code>, <code>20m</code>, or <code>1h</code>.</span>
            <code>--max-files N</code><span>Maximum files per repository; default <code>100000</code>.</span> <code>--max-file-size BYTES</code
            ><span>Maximum bytes read from one file; default <code>52428800</code> (50 MiB).</span> <code>--detail MODE</code
            ><span><code>summary</code>, <code>review</code> (default), or <code>all</code> controls displayed detail.</span> <code>--progress MODE</code
            ><span><code>auto</code> (default), <code>plain</code>, or <code>quiet</code>. JSON and SARIF default to quiet progress.</span>
            <code>--color MODE</code
            ><span><code>auto</code> (default), <code>always</code>, or <code>never</code>. <code>NO_COLOR</code> is honored in auto mode.</span>
            <code>--min-severity LEVEL</code
            ><span
              >Display <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code>, <code>high</code>, or <code>critical</code> and above; default <code>low</code>. Presentation
              only.</span
            >
            <code>--min-confidence LEVEL</code
            ><span>Display <code>low</code>, <code>medium</code>, or <code>high</code> confidence and above; default <code>low</code>. Presentation only.</span>
            <code>--group-by FIELD</code><span>Group terminal output by <code>severity</code> (default), <code>file</code>, or <code>rule</code>.</span>
          </div>
          <p>
            Display filters do not hide findings from the verdict or change the exit policy. Use
            <code>--fail-on</code> for policy.
          </p>
          <p>
            File and archive limits apply after remote checkout. Host-mode Git cloning has a per-repository timeout but no byte or disk quota before checkout;
            <code>--max-files</code> and <code>--max-file-size</code> do not limit clone storage.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="recipes" data-search="recipes html json sarif ci docker dependency detail">
          <h2>Copyable scan recipes</h2>
          <div class="recipe-grid">
            <article>
              <h3>Save a private review</h3>
              <code>repyy scan ./checkout --format html --output review.html</code
              ><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan ./checkout --format html --output review.html">Copy command</button>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Archive structured evidence</h3>
              <code>repyy scan ./checkout --format json --output scan.json</code
              ><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan ./checkout --format json --output scan.json">Copy command</button>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Save SARIF in CI</h3>
              <p>Use medium severity as the failure threshold.</p>
              <code>repyy scan . --format sarif --output repyy.sarif --fail-on medium --progress quiet --color never</code
              ><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan . --format sarif --output repyy.sarif --fail-on medium --progress quiet --color never">
                Copy command
              </button>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Scan with Docker</h3>
              <p>Pull and verify the matching release image first.</p>
              <code>repyy scan ./repo --sandbox docker --format html --output report.html</code
              ><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan ./repo --sandbox docker --format html --output report.html">Copy command</button>
            </article>
            <article>
              <h3>Include dependencies</h3>
              <p>Group findings by file.</p>
              <code>repyy scan . --include-dependencies --detail all --group-by file</code
              ><button type="button" data-copy="repyy scan . --include-dependencies --detail all --group-by file">Copy command</button>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="reports" data-search="report formats terminal json sarif html output stdout offline code scanning">
          <h2>Choose a report format</h2>
          <div class="docs-table" role="table" aria-label="Scan report formats">
            <div role="row"><b role="rowheader">tui</b><span role="cell">Interactive terminal review</span><code role="cell">--format tui</code></div>
            <div role="row"><b role="rowheader">terminal</b><span role="cell">Prioritized human review</span><code role="cell">--format terminal</code></div>
            <div role="row"><b role="rowheader">json</b><span role="cell">Automation and archival input</span><code role="cell">--format json</code></div>
            <div role="row"><b role="rowheader">sarif</b><span role="cell">Code-scanning integrations</span><code role="cell">--format sarif</code></div>
            <div role="row"><b role="rowheader">html</b><span role="cell">Self-contained offline review</span><code role="cell">--format html</code></div>
          </div>
          <p>
            Without <code>--output</code>, text and file formats write to stdout. HTML and JSON are most useful as saved files. SARIF is a portable interchange
            format for code-scanning tools.
          </p>
          <p>
            Reports record the scan mode for each repository. Remote reports also include the fetched revision.
          </p>
          <p>
            Terminal and HTML reports use human-readable statuses; schema-1 JSON keeps machine verdict values. See the
            <a href="../trust/#incomplete-scans-and-exit-codes">status mapping</a>.
          </p>
          <div class="docs-note">
            <strong>Report privacy</strong>
            <p>
              Reports redact recognized credential patterns and can still contain paths and source evidence. Review a report before sharing it.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="report-command" data-search="report command existing json stdin render html terminal sarif filters">
          <h2>Render a saved JSON report</h2>
          <p>
            <code>repyy report</code> reads a repyy JSON scan without rescanning source. Pass a JSON file, use <code>-</code> for standard input, or run
            <code>repyy report</code> in an interactive terminal to open the report picker. A saved file opens in the interactive review by default in a
            terminal session. Noninteractive output defaults to HTML.
          </p>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Render HTML</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy report scan.json --format html --output review.html">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy report scan.json --format html --output review.html</code>
          </div>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div>
              <span>Render from stdin</span><button type="button" data-copy="cat scan.json | repyy report - --format sarif --output results.sarif">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <code>cat scan.json | repyy report - --format sarif --output results.sarif</code>
          </div>
          <p>
            Report options are <code>--format terminal|html|sarif|tui</code>, <code>--output PATH</code>, <code>--detail summary|review|all</code>,
            <code>--color auto|always|never</code>, <code>--min-severity</code>, <code>--min-confidence</code>, and <code>--group-by severity|file|rule</code>.
            Filters affect presentation only. Input must be valid repyy JSON no larger than 64 MiB; repyy rejects a verdict that conflicts with findings or
            coverage. Rendering returns code <code>2</code> for incomplete coverage, <code>1</code> for a high or critical finding, and
            <code>0</code> otherwise. Invalid input returns <code>3</code>.
          </p>
          <p>
            Only render JSON from a scan you trust. Verdict validation catches contradictions inside a report, but JSON is not signed and cannot reveal findings
            removed before someone shares it.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="rules" data-search="rules validate check list explain format json rule id">
          <h2>Rules commands</h2>
          <div class="docs-table compact" role="table" aria-label="Rules commands">
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader"><code>repyy rules validate FILE</code></b
              ><span role="cell">Validate trusted YAML, custom rules, regexes, and suppressions without scanning.</span>
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader"><code>repyy rules check</code></b
              ><span role="cell">Show built-in ruleset and intelligence snapshot status offline.</span>
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader"><code>repyy rules list</code></b
              ><span role="cell">List active indicators; add <code>--format json</code> for machine-readable output.</span>
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader"><code>repyy rules catalog</code></b
              ><span role="cell">List built-in behavioral rules; add <code>--format json</code> for the versioned catalog. <a href="/rules/">Browse the reference</a>.</span>
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader"><code>repyy rules explain RULE-ID</code></b
              ><span role="cell">Show rationale, scope, legitimate-use context, and review guidance; supports <code>--format json</code>.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Explain a finding rule</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy rules explain EXEC-001">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy rules explain EXEC-001</code>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="intel" data-search="intel intelligence status update rollback signed snapshot cache">
          <h2>Intelligence commands</h2>
          <p>Check the active snapshot and its date. <a href="../intelligence/">Intelligence setup and update instructions</a>.</p>
          <div class="docs-table compact" role="table" aria-label="Intelligence commands">
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader"><code>repyy intel status</code></b
              ><span role="cell">Show active snapshot version, age, and source; supports <code>--format json</code>.</span>
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader"><code>repyy intel update</code></b
              ><span role="cell">Explicitly download and verify a signed public snapshot.</span>
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader"><code>repyy intel rollback</code></b
              ><span role="cell">Restore the previous verified cached snapshot.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="docs-command">
            <div><span>Check the active snapshot</span><button type="button" data-copy="repyy intel status">Copy</button></div>
            <code>repyy intel status</code>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="docs-section docs-searchable" id="exit-codes" data-search="exit codes zero one two three verdict incomplete fail threshold invalid">
          <h2>Exit codes and verdicts</h2>
          <p>Use the exit code in scripts and check the report for findings and coverage.</p>
          <div class="exit-grid">
            <div>
              <strong>0</strong
              ><span>No finding reached <code>--fail-on</code> and no runtime scan error occurred. Lower-severity findings may still exist.</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>1</strong><span>A finding reached the configured <code>--fail-on</code> threshold.</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>2</strong><span>A target was not fully scanned or another runtime error occurred. In a mixed scan, this takes priority over code 1.</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>3</strong><span>The command, flag, report input, or configuration was invalid; Docker preflight errors stop before scanning.</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <strong>130</strong><span>An interactive scan or report was canceled.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            In a multi-target run, successful targets remain visible when another target is incomplete. Treat <code>SCAN INCOMPLETE</code> as unresolved
            coverage. <code>repyy report</code> uses the default high threshold when rendering saved scans.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section
          class="docs-section docs-searchable"
          id="troubleshooting"
          data-search="troubleshooting command not found remote git docker incomplete path html"
        >
          <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>
          <div class="docs-table compact" role="table" aria-label="CLI troubleshooting">
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader">Command not found</b
              ><span role="cell">Open a new terminal after installation. Check <code>command -v repyy</code> or <code>where.exe repyy</code>.</span>
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader">Remote URL fails</b
              ><span role="cell">Check <code>git --version</code>, the URL, and the matching provider token. Never put credentials in the URL.</span>
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader">Docker preflight fails</b
              ><span role="cell"
                >Start Docker, pull the digest from the matching release, and verify its signature. repyy does not fall back to host mode.</span
              >
            </div>
            <div role="row">
              <b role="rowheader">Incomplete scan</b
              ><span role="cell">Read the target error and check permissions, timeout, file/archive limits, and sandbox mounts before rerunning.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>
            Need trusted rules or suppressions? Follow the
            <a href="../configuration/">configuration walkthrough ↗</a>. For installation and sandbox setup, return to the
            <a href="../docs/">documentation home ↗</a>.
          </p>
        </section>
</DocsLayout>

<style>
  .terminal-review-examples {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 16rem), 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-block: 1.5rem;
  }

  .terminal-review-examples figure {
    min-inline-size: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .terminal-review-examples figcaption {
    margin-block-end: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .terminal-review-screenshot {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    border-radius: 0;
  }
</style>
